  "support": "A naturally tapering pebble of very hard stone, perhaps calcareous tuff. It measures 13 cm in maximum length, \n                                        3.8 cm in maximum width and approximately 1.8 cm in maximum thickness, and weighs 187.392 g. \n                                        It is complete apart from minor chipping and shows no visible traces of wear. The inscription occupies one face. \n                                        The opposite face bears a carefully cut square recess, 2 cm wide and only a few millimetres deep, containing three shallow \n                                        holes that do not pierce the stone.",
